Title: How can zod date type accept ISO date strings?.
Body: <p>When defining a schema with zod, how do I use a date type?</p>
<p>If I use <code>z.date()</code> (see below) the date object is serialized to a ISO date string. But then if I try to parse it back with zod, the validator fails because a string is not a date.</p>
<pre><code>import { z } from &quot;zod&quot;

const someTypeSchema = z.object({
    t: z.date(),
})
type SomeType = z.infer&lt;typeof someTypeSchema&gt;

function main() {
    const obj1: SomeType = {
        t: new Date(),
    }
    const stringified = JSON.stringify(obj1)
    console.log(stringified)
    const parsed = JSON.parse(stringified)
    const validated = someTypeSchema.parse(parsed) // &lt;- Throws error! &quot;Expected date, received string&quot;
