<p>Any advise on how it's possible? If possible at all</p>

Title: In Android Compose, how do I make button align to the bottom of the screen, but still remain at the bottom of scrollable content?.
Body: <p>I have my content in a scrollable Column. I want to put some buttons at the bottom of the screen if there is not enough content to scroll, while being at the bottom of the scrollable content. I've been trying Spacers and weights, but nothing seems to be working.</p>
<p>This is my test code.</p>
<pre><code>@Composable
fun TestScrollableContentWithButton() {
    var numItems by remember { mutableStateOf(20) }
    Column(modifier = Modifier.verticalScroll(rememberScrollState())) {
        ScrollableContent(numItems = numItems)
        Row(
            modifier = Modifier
                .fillMaxWidth()
                .padding(bottom = 20.dp),
            horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.SpaceEvenly
        ) {
            Button(onClick = { numItems++ }) { Text(&quot;Add Item&quot;) }
            Button(onClick = { numItems = 0 }) { Text(&quot;Clear Items&quot;) }
        }
    }
}

@Composable
fun ScrollableContent(modifier: Modifier = Modifier, numItems: Int) {
    repeat(numItems) {
        Text(modifier = Modifier.padding(20.dp), text = &quot;Test Text $it&quot;)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>And here are some sample images showing how the code behaves. In the first image, the red outline is what I want to happen. The buttons should stick to the bottom of the screen if there is not enough content to scroll. The second image shows that the buttons are visible if the user has scrolled all the way to the bottom.
<a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/A8CQE.jpg" rel="noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/A8CQE.jpg" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>EDIT: For clarity, this is a 3rd image showing that the buttons are not visible until the user is scrolled all the way to the bottom.</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/nMhJl.jpg" rel="noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/nMhJl.jpg" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>The second and third images are the correct and current behavior of the code. Only the first image contains what I want to happen.</p>
<p>I remade this in regular xml to show what I want.
<a href="https://i.imgur.com/k30A4mj.mp4" rel="noreferrer">https://i.imgur.com/k30A4mj.mp4</a>
