Title: Mongodb/Mongoose fields and data still accessible after using $unset.
Body: <p>I am trying to remove a user if they have not verified their email after a certain time with mongoose. So I am setting a field called <code>verifyBy</code> to a date and giving it an expires time. then when the user verifies the email I am removing it with unset. This seems to be working. I can't see the field when looking in Mongodb Compass and the user doesn't expire so it seems to be unsetting the field.</p>
<p>The issue is I want to check if the user is verified before they login. So when I do this check I am still able to access the <code>verifyBy</code> field. Here is my user model:</p>
<pre><code>const Schema = mongoose.Schema

const UserSchema = new Schema({
  name: {
    type: String,
    required: true,
  },
  email: {
    type: String,
    required: true,
    unique: true,
  },
  password: {
    type: String,
    required: true,
  },
  verifyBy: {
    type: Date,
    expires: '2m',
    default: Date.now,
  },
  register_date: {
    type: Date,
    default: Date.now,
  },
})

const User = mongoose.model('user', UserSchema)

export default User
</code></pre>
<p>Then in my verification route I am doing this to unset the field:</p>
<pre><code>const user = await User.findOneAndUpdate(
  { _id },
  { $unset: { verifyBy: 1 } }
)
</code></pre>
<p>This seems to work because in Compass you can see the <code>verifyBy</code> field is gone. Also the user is not removed now after the allotted time so at this point everything seems to be working.</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/FKxjD.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/FKxjD.png" alt="Mongodb Compass Image" /></a></p>
<p>But then after all of this in my login route I want to check and see if the <code>verifyBy</code> field is still set before the user logs in and it is still set and accessible. Below in my login I do:</p>
<pre><code>const user = await User.findOne({ email: email })
console.log('verifyBy', user?.verifyBy)
</code></pre>
<p>And as you can see by the console log the <code>verifyBy</code> field is still there and accessible.</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/PONlJ.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/PONlJ.png" alt="Console log image" /></a></p>
<p>I could just set another field called <code>verified</code> or something and just set that to true when the user verifies their email but I shouldn't have to if the <code>verifiedBy</code> field is not set. And what good does it do to unset something if it is still accessible by code. I feel like I am not doing something right but I'm not sure what.</p>

