</code></pre>
<p>I added it to the <code>package.json</code> line <code>&quot;type&quot;: &quot;module&quot;</code></p>
<pre><code>webpack.config.ts
import * as path         from 'path';
import * as webpack      from 'webpack';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'url';

const __dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));

const PATHS = {
  entry:  path.resolve(__dirname, 'src/server/index.ts'),
  output: path.resolve(__dirname, 'dist'),
};

const config: webpack.Configuration = {
  target:  'node',
  entry:   PATHS.entry,
  output:  {
    path:     PATHS.output,
    filename: 'bundle.js',
  },
  module:  {
    rules: [
      {
        test:    /\.ts(x?)$/,
        use:     'ts-loader',
        exclude: '/node_modules/',
      },
    ],
  },
  resolve: {
    extensions: ['*', '.js', '.jsx', '.json', '.ts', '.tsx'],
  },
};

export default config;
</code></pre>
<p>By running the  command <code>&quot;build&quot;: &quot;webpack --config config/webpack.config.ts --mode development&quot;</code>, I get an error :</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[webpack-cli] Failed to load
'/node_esm/webpack.config.ts' config
[webpack-cli] TypeError [ERR_UNKNOWN_FILE_EXTENSION]: Unknown file
extension &quot;.ts&quot; for
/node_esm/webpack.config.ts</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I tried adding to my <code>config.json</code> <code>&quot;ts-node&quot;: { &quot;esm&quot;: true}</code> this didn't help solve my problem. What do I need to do in order to build an application using webpack?</p>
<ul>
