Title: Cannot access body in a HTTP post through NextJS.
Body: <p>I think I'm missing something obvious, but I need another head to get me unstuck.</p>
<p>My objective: get access to the body of a POST request as shown in this page from nextjs.
<a href="https://nextjs.org/docs/pages/building-your-application/data-fetching/building-forms" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://nextjs.org/docs/pages/building-your-application/data-fetching/building-forms</a></p>
<pre><code>// root folder page.js file
//===========================

import Image from 'next/image'
import styles from './page.module.css'

export default function Home() {
  return (
 &lt;main className={styles.main}&gt;
    &lt;div className={styles.description}&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            &lt;form action=&quot;/route&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;
                &lt;label for=&quot;first&quot;&gt;First name:&lt;/label&gt;
                &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;first&quot; name=&quot;first&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
                &lt;label for=&quot;last&quot;&gt;Last name:&lt;/label&gt;
                &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;last&quot; name=&quot;last&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
                &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Submit&quot;/&gt;
            &lt;/form&gt;
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;
  )
}
</code></pre>
<pre><code>// /response/response.js
// ===========================
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';

export async function GET(req, res) {
    console.log(&quot;====GET====&quot;);
    console.log(req.body);
    return NextResponse.json(&quot;get&quot;);
}

export async function POST(req) {
    const body = req.body;
    console.log(body);
  return NextResponse.json(&quot;post&quot;);
}
</code></pre>
<p>I fill out the form, and the browser routes correctly to the 'post' response, and the 'get' response lists when I submit.  However, on the server side, the response body is logged:</p>
<p><code>ReadableStream { locked: false, state: 'readable', supportsBYOB: false }</code></p>
<p>When I read the link, and all other documentation on nextjs and handling POST requests, the contents of the post as if it's an object, and not a readable stream.  Furthermore, I can't find anything on nextjs's website showing how to decode the readable stream, which seems a bit extensive of a solution for a common task.</p>
<p>I'm pretty sure I'm missing some mundane detail, like putting a decimal point in the wrong place, but I need help finding it.</p>
<p>Thanks a bunch peoples!</p>
<p>Chris Roode</p>

Title: How to get the file object from a (SvelteKit) POST action? (TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading &#39;byteLength&#39;)).
Body: <p>Right now, to get the file from a file input in a <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>, I am preventing the default acting when submitting and call <code>const file = event.target[0].files[0];</code>. From here I can use the file to upload it to Firebase for example, no problem.</p>
<p>My problem is I actually want to move my component to a route with a <code>+page.server.ts</code> to handle the form action, so to get the value from the POSTed form, I have this:</p>
<p>+page.svelte:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot; action=&quot;?/uploadPDF&quot; use:enhance enctype=&quot;multipart/form-data&quot;&gt;
    &lt;label for=&quot;formFile&quot; class=&quot;form-label&quot;&gt;Upload new file&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;input class=&quot;form-control&quot; type=&quot;file&quot; accept=&quot;.pdf&quot; id=&quot;formFile&quot; name=&quot;path&quot; /&gt;

    &lt;div class=&quot;form-input&quot;&gt;
        &lt;label for=&quot;password&quot; class=&quot;form-label&quot;&gt;Password&lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;input class=&quot;form-control&quot; type=&quot;password&quot; id=&quot;password&quot; name=&quot;password&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary my-3&quot;&gt;Upload&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>+page.server.ts:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export const actions = {
  uploadPDF: async ({ cookies, request }) =&gt; {
    const data = await request.formData();
    const file = data.get('path');

    console.log(file);

    return { success: true };
  },
} satisfies Actions;
</code></pre>
<p>But the log is always empty...</p>
<p>After some looking around I eventually found that <code>const file</code> could either be a File or a string, so to continue working on it I should check its instance like this:</p>
<p>+page.server.ts:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export const actions = {
  uploadPDF: async ({ cookies, request }) =&gt; {
    const data = await request.formData();
    const file = data.get('path');

    if(file instance File) {
      console.log(file);
    }

    return { success: true };
  },
} satisfies Actions;
</code></pre>
<p>This way at least it prints an object. But when I hand it over to Firestore's <code>uploadBytes()</code> it still does not work (<strong>TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'byteLength')</strong>) - other than when using <code>on:submit()</code> and <code>const file = event.target[0].files[0];</code> ....</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const uploadRef = ref(storage, `Vereinsblatt/soli_info_${yearFrom}_${seasonFrom}.pdf`);
await uploadBytes(uploadRef, file)
</code></pre>
<p>So how can I properly get the file object here - or create one?</p>
<p>(I' ve also tried to create one with <code>new File([file],&quot;myFile.pdf&quot;)</code> or <code>new Blob([path])</code> but it was not possible neither.)</p>

