  digest: 'NEXT_REDIRECT;replace;/dashboard'
}
</code></pre>
<p>When I get get rid of the try catch everything works fine:</p>
<pre><code>export async function GET(req: Request) {
  redirect('/dashboard')
}
</code></pre>
<p>This works as expected. I need try and catch because this is an auth route and I need some error handling because the request could fail, I have left out the auth functionalities becuase I realized that this happens just on a simple try and catch.</p>
<p>Or if Next 13 has another way of error handling in /api routes please let me know.</p>

