Title: How to Pass Data from Next.js Middleware to getServerSideProps in the Initial Request? (with cookies).
Body: <p>I'm facing an issue in a Next.js application (for a code callenge)</p>
<p>Here's the general flow I'm asked to achieve, specifically:</p>
<ol>
<li>In Next middleware function, check if a cookie with geolocation data exists. If not, make a call to get the data and store it in a cookie.</li>
<li>In <code>getServerSideProps</code>, utilize the cookie (if available) to pass geolocation data as a prop to my component.</li>
</ol>
<p>My current implementation sets the cookie in middleware but getServerSideProps cannot access it during the initial render/request. If I refresh the page/subsequent calls, I can read the cookie in SSR no problem.</p>
<p><strong>ChatGPT says that:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>When the user first visits the site, your middleware correctly
identifies that there is no cookie set, fetches the geolocation data,
and sets the cookie in the response. The issue arises in that during
this initial visit, the getServerSideProps function runs after the
middleware but before the cookie can be received by the client and
sent back with subsequent requests.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Below is the relevant portion of my code:</p>
<p><strong>Middleware:</strong></p>
<pre><code>export async function middleware(req: NextRequest) {
  console.log('Middleware execution!')
  if (req.cookies.has(USER_GEOLOCATION_DATA_COOKIE_KEY)) {
    console.log('Middleware: Cookie detected')
    NextResponse.next()
  } else {
    console.log('Middleware: executing call!')
    const response = NextResponse.next()
    let userGeolocationData = await getUserGeolocationData()
    console.log('Has already finished call')
    response.cookies.set(
      USER_GEOLOCATION_DATA_COOKIE_KEY,
      JSON.stringify(userGeolocationData),
    )
    return response
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>ServerSideProps of index page:</strong></p>
<pre><code>export const getServerSideProps = (async ({ req }) =&gt; {
  const userGeolocationDataCookie =
    req.cookies[USER_GEOLOCATION_DATA_COOKIE_KEY]

  let userGeolocationData

  if (userGeolocationDataCookie) {
    console.log('Habemus cookie SSR')
    userGeolocationData = JSON.parse(userGeolocationDataCookie)
  } else {
    console.log('NO COOKIE SSR')
    userGeolocationData = null
  }

  return {
    props: { userGeolocationData },
  }
}) satisfies GetServerSideProps&lt;RootPageProps&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Constraint:</strong> One can suggest that if I can't get the cookie in SSR, then I should fetch the geolocationData and return that, ensuring that the data will be sent first render. However, we discussed with the interviewer that in that case, in the initial render, I will make 2 calls, one in middleware and one in SSR. So if a million users request our page then 2 millions call will be made. So I need to look an efficient way to solve this.</p>
<p>There is a potential solution?</p>

