Title: prevent iframe scroll to the bottom of parent document.
Body: <p>I have an <code>iframe</code> in the footer of the page. When I load the page it scrolls to the <strong>bottom</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>What I have tried:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><p>I tried <code>loading=&quot;lazy&quot;</code> to make the <code>iframe</code> load when the user scrolls down but it triggers too early and jumps down to the iframe which confuses the user.</p>
</li>
<li><p>I have tried <code>onload</code> attribute to scroll up when <code>iframe</code> is loaded but it gives me the ugly effect of scrolling down first and then up because the iframes take <strong>3 sec to load</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li><p>I also tried this <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/15793882/15113491">solution</a> without any success:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>window.onload = function() {
    // blur the iframe
    document.getElementById("bing").blur();
    // set focus on #foo
