Title: Chrome Extension Authentication with ReactJS.
Body: <p>Im trying to build a chrome extension with ReactJS that also has authentication. Ive followed the google oauth flow here <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/mv3/tut_oauth/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/mv3/tut_oauth/</a> and I continuously get undefined on the token. <code>Welcome.tsx:14 Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'getAuthToken')</code></p>
<pre><code>const Welcome = () =&gt; {

  const handleAuth = () =&gt; {
    console.log('chrome', chrome)
    chrome.identity.getAuthToken({interactive: true}, function(token) {
      console.log(token);
    });
  }

  return( 
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;Typography&gt;
        Hello World
    &lt;/Typography&gt;
    &lt;Button variant=&quot;contained&quot; onClick={handleAuth}&gt;Log In Google&lt;/Button&gt;

  &lt;/div&gt;
  )
}

export default Welcome;
</code></pre>
<p>Is this because I need to use this as sort of a background script to handle it? Note my manifest has the <code>key</code> <code> &quot;permissions&quot;: [&quot;identity&quot;],</code> and the oauth2 configured correctly. Any guidance appreciated</p>

