Title: How to load components dynamically without their Host Wrapper Tag.
Body: <p>I'm loading component template during Drop Event using <code>&quot;createComponent()&quot; method of ViewContainerRef class</code>. all works okay but it loads component with it's Host Wrapper (selector) tag. but I want to load component dynamically without its Host wrapper tag.</p>
<p>here is <a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-version-hhnrtf?devToolsHeight=33&amp;file=src%2Fapp%2FpageBuild%2Fdirectives%2Fdynamic-component-loader.directive.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><strong>my stackblitz url. You can Test This on stackblitz</strong></a></p>
<p>We can load component using <code>&quot;createEmbeddedView&quot;</code> method of ViewContainerRef class.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>page-container.component.html</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;page-container&quot; appDropable [element]=&quot;element&quot;&gt;
    &lt;ng-template *ngFor=&quot;let elemData of elementData?.content; let i = index&quot; [type]=&quot;elemData.type&quot; appDynamicComponent&gt;
    &lt;/ng-template&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>dynamic-component.directive.ts</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>import { ComponentFactoryResolver, ComponentRef, Directive, Input, OnInit, Type, ViewContainerRef } from '@angular/core';
import { ContainerComponent } from 'src/app/components/elements/simple-container/container.component';
import { LabelComponent } from 'src/app/components/elements/label/label.component';

export type ElementType = 'LabelComponent' | 'ContainerComponent';

@Directive({
  selector: '[appDynamicComponent]',
})
export class DynamicComponentDirective implements OnInit {

  elementType: ElementType | undefined;

  appComponents: { [key in ElementType]: Type&lt;any&gt; } = {
    'LabelComponent': LabelComponent,
    'ContainerComponent': ContainerComponent,
  };


  @Input('type')
  set elemType(type: ElementType) {
    this.elementType = type;
  }

  componentRef: undefined | ComponentRef&lt;any&gt;;

  constructor(private componentFactoryResolver: ComponentFactoryResolver, private viewContainerRef: ViewContainerRef) { }

  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.loadComponent();
  }

  loadComponent() {
    if (this.elementType) {
      const componentElemType = this.appComponents[this.elementType];
      const componentFactory = this.componentFactoryResolver.resolveComponentFactory(componentElemType);
      if (componentFactory) {
        this.componentRef = this.viewContainerRef.createComponent(componentFactory);
        //console.log(&quot;Created Component&quot;, this.elementType)
        //console.log(this.componentRef.instance)
      }
    }
  }
}

</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>label.component.html</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>&lt;ng-template #childComponentTemplate&gt;
&lt;label&gt;
    This is my Label
&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;/ng-template&gt;
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>label.component.ts</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>import { Component, OnInit, TemplateRef, ViewChild, ViewContainerRef } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-label',
  templateUrl: './label.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./label.component.scss']
})
export class LabelComponent implements OnInit {

  @ViewChild('childComponentTemplate', { static: true }) childComponentTemplate!: TemplateRef&lt;any&gt;;

  constructor(private viewContainerRef: ViewContainerRef) { }

  ngOnInit(): void {
    console.log(this.childComponentTemplate);
    this.viewContainerRef.createEmbeddedView(this.childComponentTemplate);
    console.log(this.viewContainerRef.element.nativeElement);

  }
}

</code></pre>
<p><strong>Description of Above Code :-</strong> elementData?.content is a array object. On Drop Event I push element Type in elementData?.content array.</p>
<p>Now when If elementData?.content not empty than dynamicComponent creating the component based of their ElementType. but viewContainerRef's createComponent() method loading component with its Host Wrapper tag.</p>
<p>for e.g. if ElementType = 'LabelComponent' than loaded component display in inspect element as like below</p>
<pre><code>&lt;app-label&gt;&lt;label&gt;This is my Label&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/app-label&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>But I want to load without its Host Tag (<code>&lt;app-label&gt;&lt;/app-label&gt;</code>)</p>
<p>that's why I deaclared ViewChild In the LabelComponent &amp; onInit Event <code>   this.viewContainerRef.createEmbeddedView(this.childComponentTemplate);</code> that ng-template referance variable pass on to createEmbeddedView method</p>
<p>Now, declaring viewChild in Labelcomponent I achieved what I need.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>My Question is :- may be this is bad idea to use createEmbeddedView() after the createComponent().</strong>. can anyone give me a better solution for load component dynamically without its host tag using Component Type.</p>
<p>Please Let me correct if I'm wrong about this use of createEmbeddedView() after loading that component using createComponent().</p>
<p>Thank You.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Updated: 18th June, 2023</strong></p>
<p>If you wish to create component dynamically as a EmbeddedView(without its host tag) then you can refer below updated code...</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>IMPORTANT NOTIC:-</strong>
If you load component as a EmbeddedView using below way. then Note that, <code>@HostListener()</code> &amp; <code>@HostBinding()</code> inside <code>WhatEverComponent.ts</code> file. even angular life cycle events (onInit, AfterViewInit, AfterViewCheck, OnDestroy etc all) also not works for <code>WhatEverComponent.ts</code> file.
But <code>@HostListener()</code> &amp; <code>@HostBinding()</code> works perfectly in &quot;Directive Class&quot;. even angular life cycle events also works perfectly. only Angular Life Cycle Event Hooks not works for WhatEverComponent.ts file if we create emebeddedView of WhatEverComponent</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>dynamic-component.directive.ts</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>import { ComponentFactoryResolver, ComponentRef, Directive, Injector, Input, OnInit, Type, ViewContainerRef } from '@angular/core';
import { ContainerComponent } from 'src/app/components/elements/simple-container/container.component';
import { LabelComponent } from 'src/app/components/elements/label/label.component';

export type ElementType = 'LabelComponent' | 'ContainerComponent';

@Directive({
  selector: '[appDynamicComponent]',
})
export class DynamicComponentDirective implements OnInit {

  elementType: ElementType | undefined;

  appComponents: { [key in ElementType]: Type&lt;any&gt; } = {
    'LabelComponent': LabelComponent,
    'ContainerComponent': ContainerComponent,
  };


  @Input('type')
  set elemType(type: ElementType) {
    this.elementType = type;
  }

  componentRef: undefined | ComponentRef&lt;any&gt;;

  constructor(private componentFactoryResolver: ComponentFactoryResolver, private viewContainerRef: ViewContainerRef, private injector: Injector) { }

  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.loadComponent();
  }

  loadComponent() {
    if (this.elementType) {
      const componentElemType = this.appComponents[this.elementType];
      const componentFactory = this.componentFactoryResolver.resolveComponentFactory(componentElemType);
      if (componentFactory) {
        this.componentRef = componentFactory.create(this.injector); // create component.
        // this.componentRef = this.viewContainerRef.createComponent(componentFactory); // create component &amp; inserts its host view into this container

        if (this.componentRef.instance.childComponentTemplate) {
          this.viewContainerRef.createEmbeddedView(this.componentRef.instance.childComponentTemplate);
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

</code></pre>
<p>here is <a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-version-hhnrtf?devToolsHeight=33&amp;file=src%2Fapp%2FpageBuild%2Fdirectives%2Fdynamic-component-loader.directive.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><strong>my stackblitz url. You can Test This on stackblitz</strong></a></p>
<p>So, <strong>My Updated QUestion</strong> is how to create EmbeddedView Dynamically without affecting life cycle event like ngOnInit, ngAfterViewInit ?</p>

Title: Undefined variable in component upon API call.
Body: <p>I'm getting a lot of my variables undefined and ran at times when they shouldn't run. My best guess is that it is related to the way I make the API call.</p>
<p>Full code - <a href="https://fennzo-advantageapi-emn793znarg.ws-us93.gitpod.io/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://fennzo-advantageapi-emn793znarg.ws-us93.gitpod.io/</a></p>
