<li><p>When I run the program, the console statements doesn't get printed on chrome but on edge??</p>
</li>
<li><p>When I start the problem I get the error <code>ERROR TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'trim')</code> in app.component.ts ngOnInit() when I try to read csv. The csv are not empty and this method works as expected to load the csv into the arrays</p>
</li>
<li><p>When I click view for Stock symbol, the chart displays as expected, but I get <code>loader.js:98 ERROR Error: Uncaught (in promise): TypeError: Cannot use 'in' operator to search for 'Time Series (5min)' in undefined</code>. In debug, I can see this line <code>console.log(&quot;data&quot;, this.data);</code> in chart.componenet.ts ran 3 times in total when it should only run once when the api call in <code>app.component.ts generate_stock_chart</code> has the data ready which then sends the data to chart.component.ts</p>
</li>
<li><p>The same problem in 3) applies for forex</p>
</li>
</ol>
