Title: Put labels on Kendo Switch.
Body: <p>I am using the Switch Component from Kendo UI for Angular. I created a switch component, but I noticed that in the Documentation the switch appears with default labels &quot;On&quot; and &quot;Off&quot; <a href="https://www.telerik.com/kendo-angular-ui/components/inputs/switch/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">default switch</a>, but my Button appeared without them. So I went to the documentation and saw the &quot;offLabel&quot; and &quot;onLabel&quot; <a href="https://www.telerik.com/kendo-angular-ui/components/inputs/api/SwitchComponent/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">properties</a>. I used them in my code but I still don't get labels.</p>
<p>component.html</p>
<pre><code>&lt;kendo-switch name=&quot;isActive&quot; onLabel=&quot;Yes&quot; offLabel=&quot;No&quot; class=&quot;switch&quot; [(ngModel)]=&quot;inspectionPlan.isActive&quot;&gt;&lt;/kendo-switch&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I opened the Browser DevTools and saw this</p>
<pre><code>&lt;span class=&quot;k-switch-label-on&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt; Yes &lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;k-switch-label-off&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt; Yes &lt;/span&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I think the labels don't appear, because of the aria-hidden property, but I don't understand why it's set by default to be hidden. Does anyone know how to remove it?</p>

