Title: How can I create a box with an angle one side and rounded corners via CSS?.
Body: <p>I currently find myself needing to make something like this.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/G2Ypw.png" alt="Enter image description here" /></p>
<p>My first thought was to use clip-path, but the rounded corners would be hard to pull off, and it would be hard to maintain the 22.5 degrees when the button changes width because of its contents.</p>
<p>So I ended up making each button two <em><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML_element#Other_block_elements" rel="noreferrer">divs</a></em>, with one div being skewed by 22.5 degrees and being overlapped by the regular rectangular div. Then I added border radius to both.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
