Title: How can I show files being downloaded in WinSCP .NET assembly from PowerShell.
Body: <p>I have a script that downloads some recordings from an FTP server and the downloads are saved in a folder inside a local path on my computer.</p>
<p>I have been able to trigger a message when all the recordings have been downloaded successfully, but I wanted instead to display a message every time each of the FTP recordings are downloaded. How can I do that?</p>
<p>This is the script:</p>
<pre><code>Add-Type -Path &quot;C:\Program Files (x86)\WinSCP\WinSCPnet.dll&quot;

$sessionOptions = New-Object WinSCP.SessionOptions -Property @{
