Title: How can I get a programmatically created dragover event to work (Javascript)?.
Body: <p>I have several drag and drop functions. I want to make certain drop targets unavailable during <code>dragover</code> based on the properties of the element being dragged over them without using global variables. However, I have not been able to find a way to access the properties of the element being dragged in the function handling the <code>dragover</code> event. I can access both during the drag function using <code>document.elementFromPoint(event.clientX, event.clientY);</code> to get the drop target. I created the <code>dragover</code> event programmatically from within the drag function and attached it to the element being dragged over, but it won't work. What am I doing wrong?</p>
