Title: Counting multiple associated entries of same model with Sequelize.
Body: <p>I have two tables, <code>transaction</code> and <code>account</code>. A <code>transaction</code> has at least one and optional a second associated <code>account</code> trough two diffrent foreign keys. <strong>Using Sequelize (6.32.0), how do I count all <code>transaction</code>s associated to <code>account</code> trough the first (id_account) or second (id_account_destination) foreign key?</strong></p>
<p>sql query to achieve:</p>
<pre><code>SELECT `account`.`id`, `account`.`name`, COUNT(`transactions`.`id`) AS `transaction_count`
    FROM  `accounts` AS `account`
    LEFT OUTER JOIN `transactions` AS `transactions`
    ON `account`.`id` = `transactions`.`id_account`
    OR `account`.`id` = `transactions`.`id_account_destination`
    GROUP BY `transactions`.`id_account`;
</code></pre>
<p>model definitions:</p>
<pre><code>// account
module.exports = (sequelize, Sequelize) =&gt; {
    return sequelize.define(&quot;account&quot;, {
        id: {
            primaryKey: true,
            type: DataTypes.UUID,
            defaultValue: DataTypes.UUIDV4
        },
        name: {
            type: DataTypes.STRING
        }
    });
};

// transaction
module.exports = (sequelize, Sequelize) =&gt; {
    return sequelize.define(&quot;transaction&quot;, {
        id: {
            primaryKey: true,
            type: DataTypes.UUID,
            defaultValue: DataTypes.UUIDV4
        },
        id_account: {
            type: DataTypes.UUID
        },
        id_account_destination: {
            type: DataTypes.UUID,
            allowNull: true
        },
        amount: {
            type: DataTypes.DOUBLE
        }
    });
};
</code></pre>
<p>model relations:</p>
<pre><code>db.transaction.belongsTo(db.accounts, { foreignKey: 'id_account', as: 'account' });
db.transaction.belongsTo(db.accounts, { foreignKey: 'id_account_destination', as: 'account_destination' });
</code></pre>
<p>working solution for counting trough one association:
<em>(still wondering why he is choosing the second association trough id_account_destination)</em></p>
<pre><code>    db.accounts.findAll({
        subQuery: false,
        attributes: {
            include: [[db.sequelize.fn('COUNT', db.sequelize.col('transactions.id')), 'transaction_count']],
        },
        include: [
            { model: db.transaction, attributes: [] }
        ],
        group: ['transactions.id_account']
    })
</code></pre>
<p>attempt with error &quot;Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'getTableName')&quot;</p>
<pre><code>    db.accounts.findAll({
        subQuery: false,
        attributes: {
            include: [[db.sequelize.fn('COUNT', db.sequelize.col('transactions.id')), 'transaction_count']],
        },
        include: [
            { model: db.transaction, attributes: [], through: 'account_destination' }
            { model: db.transaction, attributes: [], through: 'account' }
        ],
        group: ['transactions.id_account']
    })
</code></pre>

