Title: How can I use vector of an abstract/interface class as function parameter?.
Body: <p>I'm trying to use a vector of an abstract/interface class <code>Base</code> as parameter to a function <code>g</code> (in <code>main.cpp</code>), so that i can pass vectors of derived classes as arguments.</p>
<p>Since I can't have instances of <code>Base</code>, I'm trying to pass vectors of unique pointers instead -- as this seems to be the preferred way to do it. However, I'm not allowed to convert from <code>vector&lt;unique_ptr&lt;Test::A&gt;&gt;</code> to <code>vector&lt;unique_ptr&lt;Test::Base&gt;&gt;</code> for some reason and I don't understand why.</p>
<p><strong>Question: why is this not allowed and how can I solve it?</strong></p>
<p><code>module.hpp</code> looks like this:</p>
<pre><code>#ifndef _MODULE_HPP
