    at dispatchEventsForPlugins (http://localhost:3000/static/js/bundle.js:15131:7)
    at http://localhost:3000/static/js/bundle.js:15291:16
</code></pre>
<p>i'm trying to learn react and struct here, I already studied official quick start guide 2-3 times, but still not able to figure out what i am doing wrong, any help will be appreciated</p>

Title: How to configure ESLint to add an empty line between same-level JSX blocks?.
Body: <p>Is there a configuration option in ESLint or any other tool that can automatically add an empty line between JSX blocks that are at the same level?</p>
<p>For example, consider the following JSX code:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;Hello /&gt;
  &lt;Hello firstName=&quot;John&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;Hello firstName=&quot;John&quot; lastName=&quot;Smith&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Is it possible to automatically format the code to achieve the following:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;Hello /&gt;

  &lt;Hello firstName=&quot;John&quot; /&gt;

  &lt;Hello firstName=&quot;John&quot; lastName=&quot;Smith&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I'm looking for a solution that can help maintain a consistent and readable code style by adding an empty line between same-level JSX blocks. It would be great if this could be achieved through a configuration option or a plugin in ESLint or any other tool.</p>

