Title: jsonwebtoken 9.0.0 - getting error: TypeError: Cannot redefine property: decode - when trying to stub.
Body: <p>so <code>npm audit</code> just found <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/jsonwebtoken" rel="nofollow noreferrer">jsonwebtoken</a> to have a security vulnerbility. <a href="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-27h2-hvpr-p74q" rel="nofollow noreferrer">The solution</a> is to update to version <code>9.0.0</code> - which I did.</p>
<p>However, my mocha tests are not passing now. During a <code>beforeEach</code>, I am trying to stub the <code>decode</code> function using <code>sinon.stub</code>, which now throws this TypeError:</p>
<p><code>TypeError: Cannot redefine property: decode</code></p>
<p>The beforeEach:</p>
<pre><code>const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

beforeEach(function () {
  this.sinon.stub(jwt, 'verify').returns({ email: 'email@email.com' });
  this.sinon.stub(jwt, 'decode').returns({ header: { alg: 'RS256', typ: 'JWT', kid: 'MOCKKID' } });
  this.sinon.stub(jwks, 'getKey').returns('some mock certificate');
  this.sinon.stub(T, 'expired');
});
</code></pre>
<p>I assume that stubbing <code>verify</code> still works, since the error only throws on the next line when I try to stub <code>decode</code></p>
<p>Yes, there is a <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/64131445/sinon-stub-throws-typeerror-cannot-redefine-property">post with similar question</a>, but it's two years old, and the accepted answer is that &quot;this is soon to be fixed in a future version&quot;. So not really relevant anymore.</p>

