Title: How to do dynamic v-model name binding in Vue.
Body: <p>In Vue2, I am using <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/vuex-map-fields" rel="nofollow noreferrer">vuex-map-fields</a> which enables two-way data binding for form fields saved in a Vuex store.</p>
<p>My map fields looks like this-</p>
<pre><code>...mapFields(&quot;myModule&quot;, {
  A_grade: &quot;obj.A_grade&quot;,
  B_grade: &quot;obj.B_grade&quot;,
}),
</code></pre>
<p>and I am using it in my template like this-</p>
<pre><code>&lt;v-select v-if=&quot;someCondition&quot; v-model=&quot;A_grade&quot; :items=&quot;items&quot;&gt;&lt;/v-select&gt;
&lt;v-select v-else v-model=&quot;B_grade&quot; :items=&quot;items&quot;&gt;&lt;/v-select&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>This is working perfectly. The only concern is I have to write this <code>v-select</code> component twice. So, to make it dynamic I tried something like this-</p>
<pre><code>// I want v-model to be resolved as 'A_grade' or 'B_grade'
&lt;v-select v-model=&quot;fit + '_grade'&quot; :items=&quot;items&quot;&gt;&lt;/v-select&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre><code>export default {
  data() {
    return {
      fit: null,
    }
  },
  computed: {
    ...mapFields(&quot;myModule&quot;, {
      A_grade: &quot;obj.A_grade&quot;,
      B_grade: &quot;obj.B_grade&quot;,
    }),
  },
  mounted() {
    this.fit = this.someCondition ? 'A' : 'B'
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>But it ends up with a syntax error-</p>
<pre><code>Assigning to rvalue
</code></pre>
<p>Eslint error-</p>
<pre><code>v-model' directives require the attribute value which is valid as LHS
</code></pre>
<p>Is there any way I can create a <code>v-model</code> from the map fields' names?</p>
<p>I set up a <strong><a href="https://codesandbox.io/s/vuex-map-fields-basic-example-forked-3005zf?file=/src/App.vue:135-147" rel="nofollow noreferrer">demo</a></strong> here. Uncomment the last input field and you should see the error.</p>

