Title: Why PhpStorm doesn&#39;t recognize methods included in a class with traits?.
Body: <p>To explain the essence of the problem, I sketched a small structure for an example, imagine that we want to interact with a certain service through api.</p>
<p>MyService folder structure:</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/frYqR.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/frYqR.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>MyService.php:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

namespace App\Services\MyService;

use App\Services\MyService\API\Api;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\App;

class MyService
{
    public Api $api;

    public function __construct()
    {
        $this-&gt;api = App::make(Api::class);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Api.php:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

namespace App\Services\MyService\API;

use App\Services\MyService\API\Interfaces;

class Api
{
    public Interfaces\UpdateCenter $updateCenter;

    public function __construct(
        Interfaces\UpdateCenter $updateCenter
    ) {
        $this-&gt;updateCenter = $updateCenter;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Interfaces\UpdateCenter.php:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

namespace App\Services\MyService\API\Interfaces;

interface UpdateCenter
{
    public function getApiVersion(): string;
}
</code></pre>
<p>UpdateCenter.php:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

namespace App\Services\MyService\API\Layers\UpdateCenter;

use App\Services\MyService\API\Layers\UpdateCenter\Methods;
use App\Services\MyService\API\Interfaces;

class UpdateCenter implements Interfaces\UpdateCenter
{
    use Methods\GetApiVersion;
}
</code></pre>
<p>GetApiVersion.php</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

namespace App\Services\MyService\API\Layers\UpdateCenter\Methods;

trait GetApiVersion
{
    public function getApiVersion(): string
    {
        return '1.0.0';
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Now here's what happens if we look at the PhpStorm hints when calling the getApiVersion() method:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

$myService = new MyService();
$versionInfo = $myService-&gt;api-&gt;updateCenter-&gt;getApiVersion('1.0.0');
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/AQNFd.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/AQNFd.png" alt="image1" /></a></p>
<p>PhpStorm can't recognize which arguments should be passed to the method, etc, but, if we remove the GetApiVersion trait and add the function directly to the UpdateCenter class:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

namespace App\Services\MyService\API\Layers\UpdateCenter;

use App\Services\MyService\API\Interfaces;

class UpdateCenter implements Interfaces\UpdateCenter
{
    public function getApiVersion(): string
    {
        return '1.0.0';
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>then phpStorm will start to recognize everything correctly:</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/WZTgN.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/WZTgN.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>It also begins to recognize if, during dependency injection, it is not an interface (abstraction) that is passed, but the Update Center class immediately:</p>
<p><strong>UPDATE:</strong>
I added an archive with an example to google drive.
<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1x6K5ocKfM_W7VVm9n9Md_LbYgm3FF6Ol/view?usp=sharing" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1x6K5ocKfM_W7VVm9n9Md_LbYgm3FF6Ol/view?usp=sharing</a></p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/T0U18.gif" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/T0U18.gif" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>

