Title: useRoute() in Vue 3 Composition API with Typescript - [Vue warn]: injection &quot;Symbol(route location)&quot; not found using Typescript and.
Body: <p>I've recently upgraded a Vue 2 app that that uses Vue Router and is mostly in typescript to Vue 3. When I migrated a function that reads the route from Options API, using this.$route to the Composition API using useRoute() the component load failed with the error:</p>
<pre><code>[Vue warn]: injection &quot;Symbol(route location)&quot; not found. 
  at &lt;Content pageName=&quot;homepage&quot; onVnodeUnmounted=fn&lt;onVnodeUnmounted&gt; ref=Ref&lt; viewRef &gt; &gt; 
  at &lt;RouterView&gt; 
  at &lt;Website&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I've stripped the app down as possible to avoid any confounding issues and here's what I'm running the gets the error.</p>
<p>I'm running with:
&quot;vue&quot;: &quot;^3.3.4&quot;,
&quot;vue-router&quot;: &quot;^4.2.1&quot;,</p>
<p>This is the entry code</p>
<pre><code>website.js
import { createApp } from &quot;vue&quot;
import router from &quot;./routes/router.js&quot;
import Website from &quot;./website.vue&quot;
const app = createApp(Website)
app.use(router)
app.mount(&quot;#shop&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>then here's the base component:</p>
<pre><code>website.vue
&lt;template lang=&quot;pug&quot;&gt;
router-view
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
import { defineComponent } from &quot;vue&quot;
export default defineComponent({
    name: &quot;Website&quot;
})
</code></pre>
<p>the router:</p>
<pre><code>router.js
import { createRouter, createWebHistory } from &quot;vue-router&quot;
import Content from &quot;../components/content.vue&quot;

const router = createRouter({
    history: createWebHistory(),
    routes: [
        {
            path: &quot;/&quot;,
            components: {
                default: Content,
                },
            props: {
                default: { pageName: &quot;homepage&quot; }
            },
    ]
})

export default router
</code></pre>
<p>then the active component that works like this in Options API:</p>
<pre><code>content.vue
&lt;template lang=&quot;pug&quot;&gt;
h1 {{ myroute.fullPath }}
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
export default {
    name: &quot;Content&quot;,
    props: {
        pageName: { 
            type: String,
            required: true
        }
    },
    computed: {
        myroute() {
            return this.$route
        }   
    }
}
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Using Composition API this works</p>
<pre><code>content.vue
&lt;template lang=&quot;pug&quot;&gt;
h1 {{ myroute.fullPath }}
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
import { useRoute } from &quot;vue-router&quot;

export default {
    name: &quot;Content&quot;,
    props: {
        pageName: { 
            type: String,
            required: true
        }
    },
    setup(props) {
        const route = useRoute()
        return {
            myroute: route
        }
    }
}
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>But when I switch to TS like this:</p>
<pre><code>content.vue
&lt;template lang=&quot;pug&quot;&gt;
h1 {{ myroute.fullPath }}
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script lang=&quot;ts&gt;
import { useRoute } from &quot;vue-router&quot;
import { defineComponent } from &quot;vue&quot;

export default defineComponent ({
    name: &quot;Content&quot;,
    props: {
        pageName: { 
            type: String,
            required: true
        }
    },
    setup(props) {
        const route = useRoute()
        return {
            myroute: route
        }
    }
})
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I get this warning:</p>
<pre><code>[Vue warn]: injection &quot;Symbol(route location)&quot; not found. 
  at &lt;Content pageName=&quot;homepage&quot; onVnodeUnmounted=fn&lt;onVnodeUnmounted&gt; ref=Ref&lt; undefined &gt; &gt; 
  at &lt;RouterView&gt; 
  at &lt;Website&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>and this error:</p>
<pre><code>Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: can't access property &quot;fullPath&quot;, $setup.myroute is undefined
</code></pre>
<p>I can't understand how switching to TS would break functioning code.</p>

Title: Why are all of my &quot;this&quot; pointers the same value?.
Body: <p>I'm working on the following code snippet:</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;                                                                                                                                                                                            
#include &lt;vector&gt;

class myclass
{
    public:
        myclass()
        {
            std::cout &lt;&lt; this &lt;&lt; std::endl;
        }
};

int main()
{
    std::vector&lt;myclass&gt; v;
    for(uint32_t i = 0; i &lt; 10; i++)
        v.push_back(myclass());
    return 0;
}
</code></pre>
<p>I'm compiling the code using <code>g++ main.cpp</code>. When I execute the compiled binary, I get:</p>
<pre><code>0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
0x7ffebb8f8cab
</code></pre>
<p>My question is why are all the <code>this</code> pointers identical? If I'm creating 10 different objects of the same class, there should be 10 distinct <code>this</code> pointers. Right?</p>
<p>As far as I understand, my code is currently using the references of the same objects to populate the vector <code>v</code>. However, what I want are 10 distinct objects of <code>myclass</code>. How can I get this? This code is a part of a larger project and that project has some issues with <code>new</code> and <code>delete</code>. So I cannot use that API. What am I doing wrong and how can I fix this?</p>

Title: Why can&#39;t we capture this in a lambda that is the default parameter of a method?.
Body: <p>I'm attempting to capture the <code>this</code> pointer within a lambda function that serves as the default parameter for a method.</p>
<p>My goal is to invoke a method of this class from within the lambda, which necessitates capturing the <code>this</code> pointer.</p>
