Title: How to use vitePreprocess with global SCSS mixins in SvelteKit?.
Body: <p>In my <a href="https://kit.svelte.dev/" rel="noreferrer">SvelteKit</a> project I am using SCSS and in order to include some mixins that are used throughout the project, I switched from <code>vitePreprocess</code> to <code>svelte-preprocess</code> and prepended them with <code>scss.prependData</code>. Now my config looks like this:</p>
<pre><code>const config = {
  preprocess: preprocess({
    scss: {
      prependData: `@import './src/styles/prepend.scss';`,
    },
  }),
  // ..
  // Other options not relevant to the question
}
</code></pre>
<p>Since <a href="https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/integrations#preprocessors" rel="noreferrer">the official SvelteKit docs</a> suggest that <code>vitePreprocess</code> <a href="https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/integrations#preprocessors-svelte-preprocess" rel="noreferrer">might be faster</a>, I was wondering if I can set up global mixins with it.</p>
<p>I tried importing <code>prepend.scss</code> in my root <code>+layout.svelte</code> file but now I'm getting an <code>Undefined mixin</code> error.</p>
<p>Can I use mixins with <code>vitePreprocess</code> or is <code>svelte-preprocess</code> the only way to achieve this at the moment?</p>

