<p>Essentially, I need the ability to create and render UI with JavaScript, CSS, HTML, and React inside Power Point slides. Creating a task panel app that renders React components inside the task panel is straightforward, but I have not found a similar method of rendering React components in slide content areas. Changing the <code>AppType</code> to <code>ContentApp</code> in the manifest.xml as recommended in the Microsoft docs renders a content area in a slide with a loading spinner that never resolves that I don't know how to manipulate.</p>
