Title: IntelliJ: Disable &quot;TS80006: This may be converted to an async function.&quot;.
Body: <p>In WebStorm, How can I disable the warning (aka. &quot;quick-fix&quot;):</p>
<pre><code>TS80006: This may be converted to an async function.
</code></pre>
<p><em>By 'warning' I mean the function name is underlined, and I see the warning text on hover:</em></p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/dopvW.png" rel="noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/dopvW.png" alt="Screenshot of the warning, incl. options" /></a></p>
<p>I would expect the setting for this warning to be under <code>Settings / Editor / Inspections</code> somewhere, but I can't find it when I search for &quot;async function&quot; or &quot;quick fix&quot; or &quot;inspections&quot;.</p>
<p><em>(I assume this setting is the same or similar in WebStorm and IntelliJ)</em></p>
<p>E.g. this warning is displayed for a function like:</p>
<pre><code>const f = (): Promise&lt;string[]&gt; =&gt; {
  return util()
    .then( mapFunction1 )
    .then( mapFunction2 );
};
</code></pre>
<p>WebStorm suggest to change it to:</p>
<pre><code>const f = async (): Promise&lt;string[]&gt; =&gt; {
  const s = await util();
  const s_1 = await mapFunction1( s );
  return mapFunction2( s_1 );
};
</code></pre>
<p>But I still prefer the <code>.then()</code> variant, as it is better readable for me.</p>
<h3>EDIT:</h3>
<p>I found the &quot;Editor / Intentions&quot; section after <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/76818795/7556457">this answer</a>, but after disabling &quot;Convert to async function&quot; the warning still appears:</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/gcSIA.png" rel="noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/gcSIA.png" alt="Screenshot of my &quot;Intentions&quot; setting" /></a></p>
<p>Interestingly, after that, &quot;Convert to async function&quot; it is not suggested anymore in the &quot;more actions&quot; menu, but the &quot;suggestion&quot; is still displayed in the code (including the hover box):</p>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/9rBkJ.png" rel="noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/9rBkJ.png" alt="Screenshot of the warning after disabling &quot;Convert to async function&quot;" /></a></p>

Title: After update of Vue 3 withDefaults throws a TypeScript error.
Body: <p>I'm trying to update version of Vue 3 (<code>3.2.x</code> -&gt; <code>3.3.x</code>).</p>
<p>But for some reason I have an error when using <code>withDefaults</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script setup lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
interface Props {
  readonly title: string;
}

// THIS WORKS
const props = defineProps&lt;Props&gt;(); 

// THIS DOESN'T WORK (guess because of withDefaults)
const props = withDefaults(defineProps&lt;Props&gt;(), { title: '' });
...
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>The error message is:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Argument type <code>DefineProps&lt;Props, BooleanKey&lt;Props&gt;&gt;</code> is not assignable to parameter type <code>DefineProps&lt;Readonly&lt;Props&gt; &amp; {}, keyof Readonly&lt;Props&gt; &amp; {}&gt;</code></p>
</blockquote>
<p>I guess I'm doing this exactly how it's <a href="https://vuejs.org/guide/typescript/composition-api.html#typing-component-props" rel="noreferrer">described in docs</a>, what's the problem here?</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Update</strong>: Looks like this issue happens only for non-boolean fields:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>
// THIS WORKS
withDefaults(defineProps&lt;{readonly foo: boolean}&gt;(), { foo: true });


// THIS DOESN'T WORK
withDefaults(defineProps&lt;{readonly foo: string}&gt;(), { foo: 'foo' });
</code></pre>

