Title: Is it possible to disable retry topic behaviour for perticular @kafkaListener method.
Body: <p>Hi there I am new to Kafka i was going through Kafka retry topic configuration without @Retryable annotations So as u know with retry topic configuration it takes main topic from @kafkaListener and make retry and dlt topic and consume all topic based on scenario.
So my question here is it possible to have retry topic behaviour for one @kafkaListener method and normal behaviour to another @kafkaListener method ?</p>
<p>Motive behind questions is to read error topic independently.</p>
<pre><code>@KafkaListener(id = &quot;foo&quot;, topics = &quot;myTopic&quot;)
    public void listen(String data) {
        System.out.println(data);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>By this i know it will read mytopic , mytopic-error , mytopic-retry  based on configuration .</p>
<p>But i want another method for just error topic like this
And to somehow disable above behaviour</p>
<pre><code>@KafkaListener(id = &quot;foo-err&quot;, topics = &quot;myTopic-error&quot;)
    public void listen(String data) {
        System.out.println(data);
    }
}
</code></pre>

Title: Does Flutter have a Listener that provides the new value directly to its listeners?.
Body: <p>I know there are <code>ValueNotifier</code>, <code>ChangeNotifier</code> and of course <code>Stream</code>, but I can't find any class that can provide the new value directly to the listeners. I could of course create my own, but I'm wondering if there is such a class &quot;built in&quot; to Flutter?</p>
<p>Example (<code>DirectValueNotifier</code> is what I'm looking for):</p>
<pre><code>class MyClass extends DirectValueNotifier&lt;String&gt;{
    void doSomething(){
        String s = DateTime.now().toIso8601String();
        notifyListeners(s);
    }
}



