Title: How to make gtag and gtm work with partytown in a react app.
Body: <p>I need some help with google analytics, gtag and gtm scripts</p>
<p>This is how I am generating the partytown snippet in webpack -&gt;</p>
<pre><code>const snippetText = partytownSnippet({
  debug: config.env !== 'production',
  forward: [
    'dataLayer.push',
    'GoogleAnalyticsObject',
    'ga',
    'gtag'
  ],
  resolveUrl: (url, _location, type) =&gt; {
    const proxyScriptHosts = [
      'www.google-analytics.com',
      'www.googletagmanager.com',
    ];
    if (type === 'script' &amp;&amp; !!url &amp;&amp; proxyScriptHosts.find((proxyScriptHost) =&gt; url.host.includes(proxyScriptHost))) {
      const proxyUrl = new URL('https://my-proxy.com/api/proxy');
      proxyUrl.searchParams.append('url', url.href);
      return proxyUrl;
    }
    return url;
  }
});
</code></pre>
